---
import '../../styles/coverage.css';
---

<section class="coverage-section section-pad">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading centered">
      <p class="label muted">What parents will learn</p>
      <h2 id="outcomes">What you will be able to decide after this webinar</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="coverage-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-index">01</span>
        <h3>Stream choice without bias</h3>
        <p>How to think about Science, Commerce and Arts without defaulting to pressure or assumptions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-index">02</span>
        <h3>Marks vs actual fit</h3>
        <p>Why high marks do not always mean Science is the right path for your child.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-index">03</span>
        <h3>Early aptitude signals</h3>
        <p>How to identify the reasoning and learning patterns that show up before stream selection pressure peaks.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-index">04</span>
        <h3>Parent-child alignment</h3>
        <p>How to reduce conflict between parent expectations and child preference during career conversations.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-index">05</span>
        <h3>NEP subject flexibility</h3>
        <p>How NEP subject flexibility affects stream and subject planning for Class 8, 9 and 10 families.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-index">06</span>
        <h3>When deeper assessment helps</h3>
        <p>When a child needs a full aptitude assessment instead of casual advice from family or coaching centres.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
